<title>NORWAY: Hafslund revises 1996 result upwards.</title>
<headline>Hafslund revises 1996 result upwards.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian power producer Hafslund ASA said it had revised upwards its pre-tax result for 1996 by 35 million crowns to 362 million crowns.</p>
<p>The company said its result after tax was increased by 36 million crowns to 291 million crowns. The full-year 1996 operating result was unchanged at 272 million crowns.  </p>
<p>Hafslund attributed the revision to results from Actinor Shipping ASA, 30 percent owned by Hafslund, which increased its net income compared with preliminary results due to a new tax regime for shipping companies in Norway.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
